From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 14:48:53 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 12/35] feat: streak coupling, AutoBiased exposure, sensor
 grain, grouped inspector

- Diffraction streak coupling: brightness saturates by f/11 so stopping
  down further reads purely as spike growth (length curve owns f/7-f/22);
  spike count follows blade physics (even N -> N, odd N -> 2N, cap 24);
  Blade Rotation turns the whole set. Save/restore like the other
  camera overrides.
- Exposure gains AutoBiased mode (new default): keeps the scene's own
  eye-adaptation window and shifts it by the camera's relative stops.
  Fixes night scenes blowing out under an absolute EV lock - the
  engine's night is artist-lit, only a few stops darker than day.
  Manual (absolute) mode retained for controlled lighting.
- Film grain baseline follows sensor size (log2(36/width) stops:
  full frame +0, APS-C +0.6, M43 +1.1, Custom by width).
- White balance diagnostic log line per temperature change.
- Both components' properties reorganised into collapsible groups
  (nested reflected structs, the same pattern as the stock engine
  components): CinematicCamera 8 groups, PhoneTracker 6 groups.
  NOTE: this changes the serialized layout - previously saved component
  values reset to defaults once on next load.

